text access mode  pull 1 40  in the pull mode  the users take the initiative to start the information access process   play video starting at  1 47 and follow transcript1 47  and in this case  a user typically would use a search engine to fulfill the goal  for example  the user may type in the query and then browse the results to find the relevant information   play video starting at  2 2 and follow transcript2 02  so this is usually appropriate for satisfying a user s ad hoc information need   play video starting at  2 10 and follow transcript2 10  an ad hoc information need is a temporary information need  for example  you want to buy a product so you suddenly have a need to read reviews about related product  but after you have cracked information  you have purchased in your product  you generally no longer need such information  so it s a temporary information need 
text access push mode in contrast in the push mode in the system would take the initiative to push the information to the user or to recommend information to the user  so in this case this is usually supported by a recommender system   play video starting at  3 13 and follow transcript3 13  now this would be appropriate if  the user has a stable information   play video starting at  3 17 and follow transcript3 17  for example you may have a research interest in some topic and that interest tends to stay for a while  so  it s rather stable  your hobby is another example of  a stable information need is such a case the system can interact with you and can learn your interest  and then to monitor the information stream  if the system hasn t seen any relevant items to your interest  the system could then take the initiative to recommend the information to you  so  for example  a news filter or news recommended system could monitor the news stream and identify interesting news to you and simply push the news articles to you   play video starting at  3 59 and follow transcript3 59  this mode of information access may be also a property that when this system has good knowledge about the users need and this happens in the search context  so for example  when you search for information on the web a search engine might infer you might be also interested in something related  formation  and they would recommend the information to you  so that just reminds you  for example  of an advertisement placed on the search page 
