wikipedia entry for zipf s law provides more context than the textbook the most frequent word will occur approximately twice as often as the second most frequent word  three times as often as the third most frequent word  etc
wikipedia entry for zipf s law provides more context than the textbook zipf s law was originally formulated in terms of quantitative linguistics  stating that given some corpus of natural language utterances  the frequency of any word is inversely proportional to its rank in the frequency table  thus the most frequent word will occur approximately twice as often as the second most frequent word  three times as often as the third most frequent word  etc 
