this article explains roc graphs  which are similar to our charting of precision and recall  these are used to evaluate classifiers  and the context of the article is medical decision making  which illustrates the diverse application of the contexts we are studying in the context of text retrieval  receiver operating characteristics  roc  graphs are a useful technique for organizing classifiers and visualizing their performance  roc graphs are commonly used in medical decision making  and in recent years have been increasingly adopted in the machine learning and data mining research communities 
an article describing multiple shortcomings and problems with the f measure  including focus on one class  bias  triangle inequality  real and predicted distributions  true negatives and poor optimization   trade offs the f measure or f score is one of the most commonly used  single number  measures in information retrieval  natural language processing and machine learning  but it is based on a mistake  and the flawed assumptions render it unsuitable for use in most contexts
a tutorial explaining how we should think about and set the beta parameter in the f measure  depending on our emphasis on precision versus recall the f measure balances the precision and recall     on some problems  we might be interested in an f measure with more attention put on precision  such as when false positives are more important to minimize  but false negatives are still important     on other problems  we might be interested in an f measure with more attention put on recall  such as when false negatives are more important to minimize  but false positives are still important     the solution is the fbeta measure     the fbeta measure measure is an abstraction of the f measure where the balance of precision and recall in the calculation of the harmonic mean is controlled by a coefficient called beta     fbeta     1   beta 2    precision   recall     beta 2   precision   recall   the choice of the beta parameter will be used in the name of the fbeta measure 
explains how to apply part of speech tagging with the nltk library the process of classifying words into their parts of speech and labeling them accordingly is known as part of speech tagging  pos tagging  or simply tagging  parts of speech are also known as word classes or lexical categories  the collection of tags used for a particular task is known as a tagset  our emphasis in this chapter is on exploiting tags  and tagging text automatically 
a simple youtube explanation of how to calculate map and gmap with detailed numerical example mean average precision  map  is the standard single number measure for comparing search algorithms  average precision  ap  is the average of  un interpolated  precision values at all ranks where relevant documents are found  ap values are then averaged over a large set of queries  either arithmetically or geometrically  gmap  
