this page gives a definition of what an inverted index is and describes how to build or construct one  an inverted index is an index data structure storing a mapping from content  such as words or numbers  to its locations in a document or a set of documents  in simple words  it is a hashmap like data structure that directs you from a word to a document or a web page 
this document gives a broad overview of information retrieval  while providing other types of indexes and search algorithm code   a forward index is a map from documents to terms  and positions   these are used when you search within a document    an inverted index is a map from terms to documents  and positions   these are used when you want to find a term in any document 
