gives an example of how to encode to gamma code and provides a calculator to check your work while you practice  elias s gamma encoding is a universal code with a prefix  the prefix indicates the length of the binary string that follows it  it is therefore possible to encode any binary integer number     to code a decimal number   n  n  take its binary representation   n     2     n 2  and calculate   l        log  2  n     l  log2 n  which is equivalent to its number of bits minus 1     example  to encode   n     5  n 5 which has for binary representation   n     2        101  n 2  101  3 bits   calculate the integer part of   log  2  5     2 32  log2 5 2 32 i e    l     2  l 2  i e  1 less than the number of bits      encode in unary   l  l and concatenate the binary representation without the most significant bit  the first 1  to obtain the elias gamma code        that corresponds to   n  n  example    l     2  l 2 is coded in unary   001  001  or sometimes   110  110  and the binary without the first   1  1 is   01  01 so the elias encoding         00101
