zipf s law in text retrieval there are many words that occur just once  let s say  in a document or once in the collection  and there are many such  it s also true that the most frequent the words in one corpus they have to be rare in another  that means although the general phenomenon is applicable  was observed in many cases that exact words that are common may vary from context to context  so this phenomena is characterized by what s called a zipf s law  this law says that the rank of a word multiplied by the frequency of the word is roughly constant 
