a very good article regarding using vector space model to compute similarities  worth reading accompany with week 01 and week 02 s lecture  computing the similarity between two text documents is a common task in nlp  with several practical applications  it has commonly been used to  for example  rank results in a search engine or recommend similar content to readers     since text similarity is a loosely defined term  we ll first have to define it for the scope of this article  after that  we ll explore two different ways of computing similarity and their pros and cons 
