implementation of page rank algorithm the pagerank algorithm outputs a probability distribution used to represent the likelihood that a person randomly clicking on links will arrive at any particular page  pagerank can be calculated for collections of documents of any size  it is assumed in several research papers that the distribution is evenly divided among all documents in the collection at the beginning of the computational process  the pagerank computations require several passes  called  iterations   through the collection to adjust approximate pagerank values to more closely reflect the theoretical true value 
