reasoning for cranfield evaluation automated evaluation  not having a user in the loop  allows us to tune systems continuously  search engines typically use the cranfield paradigm for automated evaluation  which uses a fixed collection of documents  a set of pre specified queries  and a set of relevance judgments  indications which documents are relevant for every query  
