definition for lexical cohesion lexical cohesion refers to the way related words are chosen to link elements of a text  there are two forms  repetition and collocation  repetition uses the same word  or synonyms  antonyms  etc  for example   which dress are you going to wear      i will wear my green frock   uses the synonyms  dress  and  frock  for lexical cohesion  collocation uses related words that typically go together or tend to repeat the same meaning  an example is the phrase  once upon a time   this is lexical cohesion 
