text classification ieee websites place cookies on your device to give you the best user experience  by using our websites  you agree to the placement of these cookies  to learn more  read our privacy policy   accept   close  typesetting math  100   skip to main content    ieee org  ieee xplore  ieee sa  ieee spectrum  more sites  cart   create account  personal sign in    browse   my settings   help     access provided by   university of illinois  sign out          advanced search  conferences  2022 ieee 5th international c     multi text classification model based on bret cnn bilstm  publisher  ieee  cite this  pdf  erzhuo xu  donghong qin  jun huang  jinbo zhang  all authors    6  full  text views    abstract  document sections  i   introduction  ii   background knowledge  iii   dambcl model  iv   experiment and result analysis  v   summary  authors  figures  references  keywords  metrics  abstract   when the bert pre trained model is used for the chinese text classification task  the internal parameters of the model are relatively fixed  in the process of training smaller data sets  it is easy to cause over fitting phenomenon  therefore  a multiple model structure based on bert cnn bilstm is proposed  in this structure  the bert model is used as the text information extractor  after the output features of bert model  multi head attention and text cnn model are used for further feature information extraction  low dimensional feature vectors with more dense semantic information are generated and spliced to improve the information entropy of text vectors  finally  the bilstm with self attention is used to extract the information of different words in text information and then classify the text information  and the loss function with flooding mechanism is used to carry out back propagation to further prevent the over fitting problem of the model on smaller data sets and enhance the generalization ability of the model  compared with the traditional bert  lstm  text cnn models  the accuracy  precision  recall and f1 measure of this model are all better than those of traditional bert  lstm and text cnn models  experiments show that the model can effectively extract the feature information from the text and improve the accuracy of the text classification task   published in  2022 ieee 5th international conference on big data and artificial intelligence  bdai   date of conference  08 10 july 2022  date added to ieee xplore  26 august 2022  isbn information   doi  10 1109 bdai56143 2022 9862653  publisher  ieee  conference location  fuzhou  china  section i introduction  the rapid growth of social media and various websites has led to an unprecedented flood of tex tual data from various sources  text data is unstructured and contains natural language structures  thus making it difficult to infer the expected information from the data  which has led to an increasing number of studies using deep learning for natural language based text classification  text classification is widely used in public opinion classification  1   intention recognition 2   reference resolution  mail fil tering 3  and other scenarios  in recent years  with the development of deep learning technology  word2vec maps text information into a low dimensional dense information ma trix by training large scale text data  which greatly reduces the computation of text information  pays attention to the logic between words  and represents text information more efficiently  which greatly promotes the application of deep learning in multi classification tasks 4   kim 5  firstly proposed the application of convolution neural network  cnn  in the construction of sentence model  and realized the application of cnn to text classification  cnn can capture the local features of space and graph neural network  gcn  can capture the global word collaborative information  but due to the structure of cnn and gnn  they both ignore the temporal correlation of text information  resulting in the loss of some important text information  literature 6 proposed a text classification met hod combining long and short memory units and attention mechanism  firstly  the preliminary features are extracted from the convolution layer  then  lstm uses three gates to store context history information  attention mechanism generates semantic code containing attention probability distribution  and emphasizes the influence of input on output  literature 7  proposed a combination of textual infor mation and textual information  and introduced the attention mechanism into the conditional random field of the bidirectional long short term memory network and the bi directional long short term memory network model  bilstm attention  based on the attention mechanism  this model is applied to named entity recognition research to obtain more textual contextual sentiment  but the lstm still suffers from vanishing gradients when dealing with longer sequences of information  to sum up  traditional text representation has problems such as sparse features  insufficient se mantics  and too high dimensions  ignoring the influence of parts of speech  bert model is a language representation model released by google in 2018  which is based on transformer architecture and obtained by training masked language model and predicting the next task  this learning method allows the model to create contextual word embedding  and better express the words in the text as semantically dense text vectors  in order to improve text representation and classification accuracy  this paper proposes a bert cnn bilstm multiple text classification model based on part of speech features  this model takes advantage of bert s natural integration into two way language model  and changes text information into dense vectors with contextual lexical meaning and multi dimensional semantics  so that subse quent models can see the above and following information of predicted words at the same time  bilstm 8  scans text information from left to right when actually generating content  cnn network extracts features through multi layer convolution kernel  which can effectively extract local key in formation and optimize the final feature expression  this paper combines the advantages of bert  cnn and bilstm in extracting text information  so that the accuracy of text classification has been greatly improved     section ii background knowledge  a  bert network  the bert 10  model is a self encoding language model improved by the transformer based 9  encoder layer proposed by google in 2018  the bert model introduces a random mask mechanism to generate a certain amount of noise in the input text to make the model more accurate  robust  but also because the introduction of the mask mechanism enables bert to have a certain error correction ability  and enables the model to have the ability to associate context     b  text cnn  cnn extracts text information features through convolutional layers  and then obtains local key information through pooling layers 11   cnn has a simple  efficient structure and strong adaptability  yang s 12 et al  proposed to introduce the attention mechanism into the basic cnn model and established three cnn based architectures  atcnn 1  atcnn 2 and atcnn 3  atcnn 1 adds an attention mechanism layer after the word embedding layer to obtain important local feature words  thereby improving the characteristics of convolution calculation  compared with traditional machine learning methods  the experimental results are greatly improved  but the text cnn network cannot effectively connect the context information for long text  and the gradient explosion or dispersion problem is very easy to occur during the model training process     c  lstm network  recurrent neural network 13  rnn  is one of the most widely used neural networks in natural language processing  the neurons in the hidden layer of rnn can store the output of the previous unit in the form of information  the hidden layer connects and communicates different lexical semantics  however  because the output at a distant moment requires more derivation operations than the near end output  it is difficult for the model to learn long distance dependencies  therefore  in order to to solve the problem that rnn is prone to gradient dispersion or gradient explosion in processing long texts  a special rnn network was proposed by hochreiter   schmidhuber in 1997 long short term memory  lstm   the basic structure of an lstm is the cell structure  it can better capture long distance information than rnn  the lstm unit is shown in fig  3       fig  1   lstm network    show all    at time t  the parts in the lstm unit are represented as follows   ftitc tctotht   wt  ht 1  xt  bf    wj  ht 1  xt  bi  tanh wc  ht 1  xt  bc  ft ct 1 it c t    wo  ht 1  xt  bo  ot tanh ct  1  2  3  4  5  6   view source    in the above formula  is the final output  o is the sigmoid activation function  tanh is the hyperbolic tangent function  the weight corresponding to w  and the bias corresponding to b     section iii dambcl model  this paper proposes a hybrid model text classification method dambcl  double attention merge bert cnn lstm  based on bert attention  text cnn  bilstm attention  the model captures text semantics from different fine grained levels  forming a simultaneous the information containing local and global semantics makes full use of the most critical and valuable information in the text information  so that the text classification effect has been further improved compared with the benchmark model  the complete model of this paper is shown in fig  4       fig  2   dambcl model    show all    a  bert pre training model to extract text information  one hot 14  representation is a very popular representation method in recent years  but the disadvantage of one hot representation is that the text vector is sparse and has weak representation ability  and the n dimensional vector can only represent n words  in the case of a large amount  the feature space will become very large  and the one hot representation cannot represent the semantic information of the text  bert s full name is bidirectional encoder representation from    transformer  it is a language model trained by google in an unsupervised manner based on the encoder part of the transformer model using a large amount of unlabeled text the feature extractor that uses the bert model as input text information is a recent a new text representation method  which can map high dimensional sparse vectors into low dimensional dense word vectors  effectively solving the problems of traditional text representation such as the curse of dimensionality  in the model constructed in this paper  a multi attention module is added after the bert model output vector to calculate the importance of the output text information  extract important information for text classification  and use multi head attention to pay attention to the difference in input information  part  calculate the important information from the input matrix in parallel  after selecting the important information of each part  and then connect the residual with the original vector of the bert model to speed up the model convergence speed and semantic information density  the specific structure is as follows shown in fig  5       fig  3   bert_multi_attention module    show all    assuming that the input word vectors are el  e2 en  the output vectors corresponding to different moments after processing by the bert pre training model are  and the formula for calculating the matching score between the output at each moment and the entire feature vector is as follows   score softmax  wq tn   wtk tn dk     wq tn   7   view source    finally  the matching score of the feature vector combined with the residual connection 15  is sent to the lstm model for classification output  the specific formula is as follows   wn layernorm score tn   view source    the vector t is the semantic vector directly output by the bert pre training model without being processed by the multi attention module  and t further improves the semantic information density for the final input into the lstm model by means of residual connection     b  cnn network  the cnn used in this paper is composed of multiple convolutional layers stacked on each other and then connected to the pooling layer and the fully connected layer  among them  the deep convolutional neural network can extract long distance text information more efficiently  the pooling layer can effectively compress the input information  and finally connect all the features through the fully connected layer  and send the output to the classifier  the dambcl model uses a multi layer convolutional neural network to extract information from the word vector to obtain the feature vector q  the dambcl model fuses the text information extracted by cnn and the output vector w of bret attention into a new vector x that contains contextual semantic information and local key information     c  lstm network introducing attention mechanism  in this paper  a self attention mechanism  self attention  is added to the output back end of the bilstm model used to calculate the importance of the output text information to the results  and to more efficiently extract important information that has a greater impact on the text classification results  the vector x is a low dimensional and dense semantic vector after fusion of the text information extracted by the bert pre training model and the deep text cnn model using the multi attention mechanism  the specific structure is shown in fig  6 below       fig  4   bilstm_self_attention module    show all    d  adding the loss function of flooding to enhance the generalization ability of the model  in this paper  the idea of quadratic descent 16   flooding  is introduced in the final loss function of the model to enhance the generalization ability of the model  the main formula is as follows               b  b 8   view source    the essential function of adding the flooding mechanism is to push the parameters to a more stable area  so that the ability of the model to resist disturbance is increased  and the generalization ability and accuracy of the model on smaller data sets are improved     section iv experiment and result analysis  a  experimental environment  in order to verify the prediction performance of the dambcl model  this model and benchmark experiments were performed on the windows10 operating system the specific environment is shown in table i    table i  experimental environment    b  the data set  the data set used in this expenment is from sogou chinese news data set  the specific data distribution is shown in table ii     table ii  data set statistics    c  training parameter setting  the specific parameter settings are shown in table iii and table iv     table iii  lstm network parameters    table iv  cnn network parameters    d  model evaluation criteria  the model in this paper uses four evaluation indicators  accuracy  acc   precision  pre   recall  rec  and f1  pre  value to evaluate the dambcl model  the confusion matrix is shown in table v     table v  confusion matrix    the formula for the accuracy rate  acc  is as follows   acc tp fntp tn fp fn 9   view source    the formula for the precision rate  pre  is as follows   pre tptp fp 10   view source    the recall rate  rec  formula is as follows   rec tptp fn 11   view source    f1 the formula is as follows   f1 2 pre recpre rec 12   view source    e  comparative experiment  in order to verify the performance of the proposed dambcl model  comparison was made with the following benchmark models under the same experimental conditions   1  lstm 17   firstly  text information was extracted with lstm and then classified by softmax   2  bilstm attention  18   firstly  bilstm attention is used to extract text information and then softmax is used for classification   3  text cnn 19   the text statements are processed by word segmentation first  and then the information words are sent into the convolutional neural network by embedding technology for classification   4  bert 20   bert pre training model is used to extract context information  and softmax layer is used to classify extracted text information   5  bert cnn  bert pre training model is used to extract text information initially  and cnn is used to extract local feature information of text and then softmax is used for classification   6  cnn lstm 21   first  cnn is used to extract local key features  then lstm is used to extract cnn output  and finally classification is performed  experimental results of dambcl and the above benchmark models on sogou open data set are shown in table vi     table vi  experimental performance of sogou data set    it can be seen from the table that dambcl model performs best among the above models in sogou news data set  greatly improving the effect of text classification  compared with lstm model  the scoring effect is improved by 14 38 percentage points  14 11 percentage points  14 39 percentage points and 15 4 percentage points respectively  the reason is that lstm model adopts sequence structure  although lstm model has the advantage of natural word order from left to right when extracting features  it cannot effectively relate context information  the extracted semantic information is incomplete when it is transmitted backwards  while dambcl model uses bert as a withholding device to effectively extract context information  and the information is complete when transmitted backwards  so the classification effect will be better  compared with bilstm attention model  the effect is improved by 12 19  11 86  12 19 and 12 9 percentage points respectively  compared with the text cnn model  the effect is increased by 11 45 percentage points  10 51 percentage points  11 44 percentage points and 12 75 percentage points  compared with the bert pre training model  the effect is increased by 3 05 percentage points  2 98 percentage points  3 06 percentage points  and 2 86 percentage points  the dambcl model uses bert with the attention mechanism as a feature extractor  and the feature vector output by the bert model is fused with the features output by the cnn and then sent to the lstm module with self attention for classification  this method combines bert  text the advantages of the cnn and lstm models for extracting information greatly enhance the density of text information  thereby improving the accuracy of the final classification results  it can be seen from fig  7 that the dambcl model is superior to its benchmark model in both the convergence speed of the validation set accuracy and the final result       fig  5   sogou chinese data set validation set accuracy    show all    it can be seen from fig  8 that the convergence speed of dambcl model in the loss function of verification set is also better than that of its benchmark model       fig  6   sogou chinese dataset validation set loss function    show all    section v summary  aiming at the problem of text classification  this paper proposes a multiple model based on bert  cnn  lstm and attention combined with residual connection and flooding quadratic descent module to improve the low rank and over fitting problems of the model text vector  first  the input text is mapped into a text matrix with dense semantic information through the bert model  and then the multi attention module and the text cnn model are used to extract the local key features of the text of the bert model  compared with other models  the advantages of dambcl model are further proved  the next stage of the research work is to consider improving the input information source of cnn module of dambcl model and the improvement of attention mechanism in the model  so as to make the model classification better and further improve the accuracy of text multi classification     authors  figures  references  keywords  metrics  more like this  distributed and randomized tensor train decomposition for feature extraction  2019 international joint conference on neural networks  ijcnn     published  2019    feature extraction based on principal component analysis for text categorization  2017 international conference on performance evaluation and modeling in wired and wireless networks  pemwn     published  2017    show more  references  1   q zhang  t z gao  x y liu et al    public environment emotion prediction model using lstm network j    sustainability  vol  12  no  4  pp  1 16  2020   show in context crossref  google scholar   2   liang yan  xiaoshan gao  xiongjie zhang and suokui chang  human robot collaboration by intention recognition using deep lstm neural network  2019   show in context google scholar   3   da xiao and meiyi jiang  malicious mail filtering and tracing system based on knn and improved lstm algrithm  2020   show in context google scholar   4   m manal and o nazlia   question classification basedon bloom s taxonomy cognitive domain using modifiedtf idf and word2vec j    plos one  vol  15  no  3  pp  e0230442  2020   show in context google scholar   5   y  kim   convolutional neural networks for sentence classification  c    proceedings of the 2014 conference on empirical methods in natural language processing  acl  pp  1746 1751  2014   show in context crossref  google scholar   6   x  bai   text classification based on lstm and attention   2018 thir teenth international conference on digital information management  icdim   pp  29 32  2018   show in context view article    google scholar   7   zhong qing and yan tang   an attention based bilstm crf for chinese named entity recognition   2020 ieee 5th international confer ence on cloud computing and big data analytics  icccbda   2020   show in context google scholar   8   g xu  y meng  x qiu et al    sentiment analysis of comment texts based on bilstm j    ieee acce