 338  2019   show in context crossref  google scholar   19   b guo  c zhang  j liu et al    improving text classification with weighted word embeddings via a multi channel textcnn model j    neurocomputing  vol  363  pp  366 374  2019   show in context crossref  google scholar   20   s mohammadi and m  chapon   investigating the performance of fine tuned text classification models based on bert c    2020 ieee 22nd international conference on high performance computing and communications  ieee 18th international conference on smart city  ieee 6th international conference on data science and systems  hpcc smartcity dss   pp  1252 1257  2020   show in context view article    google scholar   21   y luan and s  lin   research on text classification based on cnn and lstm c    2019 ieee international conference on artificial intelligence and computer applications  icaica   pp  352 355  2019   show in context view article    google scholar   ieee personal account  change username password  purchase details  payment options  view purchased documents  profile information  communications preferences  profession and education  technical interests  need help   us   canada   1 800 678 4333  worldwide   1 732 981 0060  contact   support  follow  about ieee xplore   contact us   help   accessibility   terms of use   nondiscrimination policy   ieee ethics reporting   sitemap   privacy   opting out of cookies    a not for profit organization  ieee is the world s largest technical professional organization dedicated to advancing technology for the benefit of humanity       copyright 2022 ieee   all rights reserved     pdf  help  
article on hierarchical agglomerative clustering hierarchical clustering algorithms are either top down or bottom up  bottom up algorithms treat each document as a singleton cluster at the outset and then successively merge  or agglomerate  pairs of clusters until all clusters have been merged into a single cluster that contains all documents  bottom up hierarchical clustering is therefore called hierarchical agglomerative clustering or hac   top down clustering requires a method for splitting a cluster  it proceeds by splitting clusters recursively until individual documents are reached  see section 17 6   hac is more frequently used in ir than top down clustering and is the main subject of this chapter 
text data ieee websites place cookies on your device to give you the best user experience  by using our websites  you agree to the placement of these cookies  to learn more  read our privacy policy  accept   close processing math  100  skip to main content  ieee org ieee xplore ieee sa ieee spectrum more sites cart  create account personal sign in ieee xplore logo   link to home browse  my settings  help   access provided by  university of illinois sign out ieee logo   link to ieee main site homepage  all  advanced search conferences  2022 ieee 5th international c    multi text classification model based on bret cnn bilstm publisher  ieee cite this pdf erzhuo xu  donghong qin  jun huang  jinbo zhang all authors  6 full text views  abstract document sections i  introduction ii  background knowledge iii  dambcl model iv  experiment and result analysis v  summary authors figures references keywords metrics abstract  when the bert pre trained model is used for the chinese text classification task  the internal parameters of the model are relatively fixed  in the process of training smaller data sets  it is easy to cause over fitting phenomenon  therefore  a multiple model structure based on bert cnn bilstm is proposed  in this structure  the bert model is used as the text information extractor  after the output features of bert model  multi head attention and text cnn model are used for further feature information extraction  low dimensional feature vectors with more dense semantic information are generated and spliced to improve the information entropy of text vectors  finally  the bilstm with self attention is used to extract the information of different words in text information and then classify the text information  and the loss function with flooding mechanism is used to carry out back propagation to further prevent the over fitting problem of the model on smaller data sets and enhance the generalization ability of the model  compared with the traditional bert  lstm  text cnn models  the accuracy  precision  recall and f1 measure of this model are all better than those of traditional bert  lstm and text cnn models  experiments show that the model can effectively extract the feature information from the text and improve the accuracy of the text classification task  published in  2022 ieee 5th international conference on big data and artificial intelligence  bdai  date of conference  08 10 july 2022 date added to ieee xplore  26 august 2022 isbn information  doi  10 1109 bdai56143 2022 9862653 publisher  ieee conference location  fuzhou  china                                         authors figures references keywords metrics more like this distributed and randomized tensor train decomposition for feature extraction 2019 international joint conference on neural networks  ijcnn   published  2019  feature extraction based on principal component analysis for text categorization 2017 international conference on performance evaluation and modeling in wired and wireless networks  pemwn   published  2017  show more references references is not available for this document  ieee personal account change username password purchase details payment options view purchased documents profile information communications preferences profession and education technical interests need help  us   canada   1 800 678 4333 worldwide   1 732 981 0060 contact   support follow about ieee xplore   contact us   help   accessibility   terms of use   nondiscrimination policy   ieee ethics reporting   sitemap   privacy   opting out of cookies  a not for profit organization  ieee is the world s largest technical professional organization dedicated to advancing technology for the benefit of humanity     copyright 2022 ieee   all rights reserved   pdf help
wikipedia page on naive bayes classifier in statistics  naive bayes classifiers are a family of simple  probabilistic classifiers  based on applying bayes  theorem with strong  naive  independence assumptions between the features  see bayes classifier   they are among the simplest bayesian network models  1  but coupled with kernel density estimation  they can achieve high accuracy levels  2  3     naive bayes classifiers are highly scalable  requiring a number of parameters linear in the number of variables  features predictors  in a learning problem  maximum likelihood training can be done by evaluating a closed form expression  4   718  which takes linear time  rather than by expensive iterative approximation as used for many other types of classifiers     in the statistics literature  naive bayes models are known under a variety of names  including simple bayes and independence bayes  5  all these names reference the use of bayes  theorem in the classifier s decision rule  but naive bayes is not  necessarily  a bayesian method  4  5 
deep learning  1 perspectives in communication  embedded systems and signal processing  pices   an international journalissn  2566 932x special issue 2022 picesjournal   publisher  worldserve online 2022  www pices journal comthis work is licensed under acreative commons attribution 4 0 international license  permissions beyond the scope of this license may be available at pices journal open access policyvisit hereto cite referthis article78abstractive text summarization using deep learningakarsh b adept  of electronics and communication  sapthagiri college ofengineering bangalore  indiadeepak kdept  of electronics and communication  sapthagiri college of engineering  bangalore  indiahemanth h mdept  of electronics and communication  sapthagiri college of engineering  bangalore  indial vishnu vardhan reddydept  of electronics and communication  sapthagiri college of engineering  bangalore  indiapadmavathi cprofessor  dept  of electronics and communication  sapthagiri college of engineering  bangalore  indiaabstract  in current era  organizing the data has been a very  tedious  process  as  there  is  a  lot  of  data  growing every  day  and  storing  and  managing  them  is  getting tougher   to  solve  this  problem  one  of  the  ways  is  to summarizing  the  data  which  in  turn  will  save  lot  of storage and makes managing data easier  in this paper we have looked into various techniques and methods to summarise the text data using deep learning techniques and   come   to   the   conclusion   that   using   encoder decoder  architecture  which  consists  of  lstms   which is   efficient   in   producing   optimum   results    this   is because  lstms  are  good  at  remembering  the  long dependencies by overcoming the problem of remembering  the  context  of  the  previous  line  in  its memory to predict the next sequence  we will first train the  model  after  setting  up  the  model  to  predict  the target  sequence   in  this  training  process   the  encoder takes an input and processes it and stores the context of that  input  whereas  the  decoder  predicts  the  next  word with  respect  to  the  previous  input   later  a  new  test input  is  uploaded  to  the  model  to  test  for  which  the target is unknown  attention mechanism is used in this model as it gives attention to the important word in the sentence to understand the context of that sentence and to generate new words from it keywords  lstms encoder decoder attentioni introductionnowadays  text  is  the  common  format  of  exchanging information   emails   reports   reviews   messages  etc are the  different  sources  of  text  data   there  are  lakhs  of reviews   is   being   given   by   customers    reporters    the information  stored  in  that  reviews  is  huge  and  it  is complicate  to  understand  the  main  content   to  resolve this  problem   we  have  to  extract  only  main  content  from the reviews text    summarization    can    be    divided    into    two approaches extractiveandabstractive the first processing step undergone by the machine is to  give  an  appropriate  score  to  every  sentence  contained in  the  datapoints  and  spots  these  sentences   in  that  the peak  sentence  will  be  taken  as  the  summary   in  this approach   there   each   sentence   will   be   grammatically correct  as  long  as  input  review  given  by  customers  is grammatically correct  so we need not to worry about the grammar   of   the   summary   generated    this   will   be important advantage for this approach in  the  abstractive  summarization  approachas  shown in  fig 1   the  review  given  is  first  understand  by  us  and hire anew language generation technique for creating the summary   on  the  use  of  otherwords  and  phrases  which are  not  there  in  the  review   this  approach  is  more  like  a human  way  of  approach   whereas  we  humans  will  not simply  choose  the  selected  sentences  for  generation  of summary  but instead of that we will make use of our own words  or  expressions  to  explain  the  main  content  of  the summary generated or text abstractive    base    approach    has    problems    and complications    so    it  becomes  least interested  inthe research  group   in  the  abstractive based  approach  we need  to  examine  the  input  reviews and new  technologies for  creating  summary   first   due  to  the  disappointing performance of already existing analysing and generating tools  will  affect  the  summarization  system  poorly   next  compared    to    extractive    summarization    abstractive summarization  is  harder  for  the  evaluation  whereasin extractive summarization  we can evaluate the flapping of the  output  summary  with  the  original  standard  summary to  check  the  output  of  the  system   but  the  abstractive summarization    will    be    having    different    ways to communicate the particular event so  it will not be a good method  due to the above mentioned reasons the most of research   group   focused   their   efforts   on   extractive summarization    and    few    of    them    on    abstractive summarization ii problemstatementin the present generation  there is enormous amount of data   generated   daily   due   to   digitalization    so    the necessity of understanding the data is important  it is very  perspectives in communication  embedded systems and signal processing  pices   an international journalissn  2566 932x special issue 2022 picesjournal   publisher  worldserve online 2022  www pices journal comthis work is licensed under acreative commons attribution 4 0 international license  permissions beyond the scope of this license may be available at pices journal open access policyvisit hereto cite referthis article79crucial  to feed the  processed data  to  the  model  for better efficiency  and  reduce  the  time  complexity   customer reviews     are     usually     prolonged     and     expressive  understanding   these   reviews   manually   is   hectic   and requires  a  lot  of  time   nowadays  people  are  busy  to completely read the reviews  this is where the intelligence of   natural   language   processing   and   deep   learning techniques   which   will   help   in   generating   abstractive summaries  iii relatedworkyuji   roh   et   al      1    machine   learning   is   used worldwide  it is very necessary to collect large quantities of data  data gathered is not completely a label data  data selection  can  be  done  as  two  steps   firstly   the  data generated  should  be  indexed  and  it  should  be  published for sharing it with others  there are several platforms for sharing the equipped datasets  there are software s for generating  data  and  storing  data   as  it  is  the  forwarding step  in  data  description   kaggle   data  world  is  some  of sites  to  visit  for  datasets   collaborative  systems  are  used to  help  us  in  making  the  work  easy   there  are  systems that  are  designed  with  dataset  sharing  in  mind   they include collaborative analysis  publishing on web vivek   agarwal   et   al      2    data   pre processing   is meant for converting raw data into a comprehensive data format  it consists of data cleaning  data integration  data transformation  and  data  reduction   real  world  data  may be  deficient   unnecessary  and  clamorous   pre processing steps include raw data  url removal  hashtag removal  emoticon    extraction     stemming     tokenization     pos tagging   parsing   processed  data   the  above  mentioned are the basic steps we must follow for every dataset  url and hashtag are used in  as it doesn t give any meaning for  the  sentences   regular  expressions  library  works  for pattern  matching  and  url  tags  detection   the  hashtag used in reviews are linking it to the accounts or shortcuts  it   is   not   necessary   for   the   model we   use   regular expressions  for  removal  of  hashtags   stemming  is  the process of reducing the preferred words into the word s stem felix  a   gers  et  al     3    alternatives  for  recurrent neural   network    i e     gated   recurrent   neural   network  gru     or    long    short term    memory     lstm      are considered  as  the  encoder  and  decoder  basic  structure  lstm s advances over traditional rnns as there is long time  gaps  for  lstm  between  the  input  events  as  that  of recurrent  neural  network   these  networks don t  extract information    it   stores   the   information    lstm   gives solution  for  highly  nonlinear  tasks   this  can  be  done  as lstms  can  learn  to  precisely  measure  time  intervals  at every time step zhenlin liang et al    4   attention mechanism is used widely  right  now  for   translation    summarization   etc   there   are   2   approaches   of   attention   namely   global attention and local attention  local attention takes limited hidden states of encoder and global attention considers all the hidden  states   the  global  attention has  a  disadvantage of to attend to all the words to source side for each target word   to  avoid this problem  we  consider  local attention in our model hai tao zheng et al    12   in this paper the attention mechanism  is  used  to  generate  news  comments   the generation of news comments is a latest  challenging and not  so  well studied  task  of  nlg   unlike  the  other  nlg tasks   the  generation  of  news  comments  requires  the contextual    correlation    between    comments    and    the respective   new    also    with   that    we   should   generate different   kinds   of   comments   to   diversify   it    because usually  people  with  different  mindset  will  have  different types  of  opinions  on  a  particular  topic  in  reality   gated attention  neural  network  model  must  be  used  to  provide the  contextual  relevance  in  generate  news  comments   to solve  the  problem  of  contextual  relevance   we  also  need to  insert  the  gated  attention  mechanism  to  use  news context  self adaptively  and  selectively   the  contextual information  from  the  news  must  be  utilized  properly  to concentrate  different  type  of  words  to  the  different  parts of the title context iv objectivesandmethodsa objectivesthe five main objectives of this project are 1 to choose an appropriate dataset 2 to pre process the data 3 to build an abstractive model 4 to  train   test  and  predict  the  model  on  different parameters 5 to translate into required language fig 1 steps for abstractive summarization modelthe above block diagram shows the steps for building an abstractive text summarization model 
regex text skip to main content      search  go to cart  log in    smart data intelligence pp 199 210cite as    regular expression based text classification using msvm and machine learning techniques  download book pdf  download book epub  regular expression based text classification using msvm and machine learning techniques  dinesh d  puri   g  k  patnaik   conference paper  first online  18 august 2022  40 accesses    part of the algorithms for intelligent systems book series  ais     abstract  due to the high popularity of patient electronic health record systems  effective data management is very essential nowadays  there are some significant volume of unstructured format data in the medical sector  computer assisted classification of such data into functional classifications such as subjects or illness may save time and money for medicine and healthcare platforms  particularly successful web healthcare providers  however  categorization in the medical sector is often difficult since even simple problems need a significant portion of domain expertise  many strategies and techniques for medical information retrieval and categorization tasks have been established during the last few decades  the general approaches are machine learning algorithms such as na ve bayes  svm and random forest  but still  those results have heavy noise in the generated regular expression and text  this paper proposes a collaborative natural language processing  nlp  and machine learning based approach to generate practical regular expressions on extensive clinical data  the first section preprocesses data with nlp algorithms such as token generation  alignment generation  key generation and patter builder  this process performs the feature extraction  and those features are carried out by module training  the modified support vector machine  msvm  and other traditional machine learning algorithms are applied to the entire test dataset  the svm produces almost 90 80 91 90  average accuracy on test data with 15 fold cross validation  in the result section  the overall experiment analysis has been demonstrated with various machine learning algorithms using a weka environment     keywords  regular expressions generation  nlp  machine learning  ml   token generation  sequence alignment  key extraction  text classification  healthcare dataset  access provided by university of illinois urbana champaign library    download conference paper pdf    1 introduction  for decades  researchers have looked at combining ml algorithms with particular rules  and rule based systems have shown to be competitive  1   to integrate rule based procedures with neural network models  two kinds of hybrid systems are created  one method relies on rules to evaluate the computer vision output  2   while another method relies on rule based algorithms to accurately identify the needed characteristics to feed machine learning models  such approaches have been investigated in the medical area to address nlp problems as clinical text categorization  3   entity extraction and connection identification  while the volume and quality of known data limit the accuracy of the developed models  particularly deep learning models  rule based object recognition efficiently uses the existing training data and offers machine learning models a significant boost  patients  narrative clinical writings for online medical counselling often include mistakes  misspellings  contractions  quasi jargons and unfinished phrases  1      natural language processing  nlp  technologies designed for regular text have a hard time comprehending the audible expression of medical terminology  4   a computerized sequence generation approach for classifying medical texts to deliver insightful and complete human like medical advice to solve these difficulties has been proposed  the system is built on a constructive nlp ml technique that has been fine tuned to fulfil the unique requirements for producing regular expression in real world applications  with a realistic dataset  the model has been shown to be capable of handling medical text categorization tasks     the rest of the work is presented under the following headings  sect  2 examines the existing methods to regular expression generating techniques created by previous researchers  while sect  3 depicts the materials and techniques employed in the creation of the proposed system  and sect  4 provides the implementing algorithm explanation  in sect  5  the experimental strategy for implementing the business work and results obtained with the technology  as well as a comparison with numerous state of the art techniques  have been discussed  section 6 details the conclusion as well as its future potential     contribution of proposed work  the previous work had the challenge of generating practical regular expressions on extensive data  and it regenerated dimensionality reduction issues and data leakage problems during classification  in this work  the entire work is evaluated in a systematic approach  including a new classification algorithm that improves the classification accuracy  and proposed sequence alignment and key generation approach to reduce the data leakage problem     2 literature survey  natural language processing  nlp  systems designed for regular text find it challenging to interpret medical phrases spoken orally  4   to address these concerns  an automated regular expression generation approach is considered for classifying medical texts in order to deliver insightful and complete human like medical assistance     1   practical studies on diverse problems in regular expression consequence     2   test general string generation from traditional phrases     3   automatic learning or synthesis of regular expressions from illustration strings or specifications     4   statically checking the syntax or specific semantic mistakes in regular expressions or verifying regular expressions with requirements     5   the representation of visual expressions     authors of paper  1  developed regex  a regular appearance feature based approach for biomedical text categorization  regex is a standard expression based approach for identifying characteristics from text documents  using the smith waterman and compensate for the lack of sequencing matching techniques  identifiers were retrieved from the medical domain and used to indicate frequent patterns  the effectiveness of the suggested approach was evaluated using three annotations datasets  including characteristics of obesity  obesity categories and smoking behaviours  features derived from consecutive sequences of characters  n grams  were utilized as a comparative  and both kinds of features were characterized mathematically using the tf idf vector framework  the capacity of background subtraction methodologies was assessed using svm and naive bayes classifiers that were trained  according to the results  regular expression features enhanced both classifications  effectiveness in all datasets despite utilizing limited functionality than n grams  particularly in datasets with knowledge on morphological attributes  in paper  4   fault based leadership development programmes were conducted for regular expression realization using mutation  a fault based strategy for generating strings suitable for regular expression testing  they provided fault classes that characterize faults that may arise when building a regular expression  as well as the idea of a distinguishing string  which is a string that may reveal a flaw  this technique  given a regular expression  generated a test suite of distinguishing strings that detected probable regular expression defects  they demonstrated several versions of the process  each with a distinct consequence in terms of test suite size and production time     regex  a simple text categorization  was turned into an al biomedical text classifier in  5  by using a query method and stopping criteria  the query approach sampled the training dataset  balancing greedy regular expression classification precision with conservative text sequence alignment classification  a stopping benchmark is a sustained condensing in the contention of query technique scores  the al classifier was considered against support vector machine  svm   naive bayes  nb  and a classifier based on bidirectional encoder models from transformers utilizing three datasets incorporating biological knowledge in spanish on smoking demeanours  obesity and obesity varieties  as regular expressions evolve over time  the qualities of regular expression edits  syntactic and semantic distinctions and feature changes of alterations were examined  in  6   two datasets were used in the investigation  to acquire the changing history of regular expressions  they first checked through the contribution logs of github applications that incorporate one in their latest iteration  second  they compiled a list of frequent terms used by research subjects during drawback tasks  regular expression matching characteristics might be dramatically different as a consequence of a one character error  regular expressions have their own range of tools that may be used to write tests  these tools display components of the pattern matching language  but not quasi sequences  recent research has looked at a fault based technique to produce regular expression tests using mutation testing  in which flaws were injected into regular expressions and strings were produced to witness the defect  resulting in non matching instances for the original regular expression     paper  7  described a constructive heuristic approach to medical text classification using regular expressions  as text classifiers  a novel constructive heuristic technique for creating a set of regular expressions might be used  the approach s key distinguishing feature was the development of a novel  regular affirmation text classifier with adequate classification performance and good interpretability  they put the system to the test using real world medical data from one of the market s major online healthcare professionals and found that it worked effectively and consistently  computer clustering techniques were employed efficiently in combination with machine learning to conduct medical text categorization tasks  and according to findings of the experiments  in  2   a new matching engine  bfa  was introduced to provide high speed mathematical equation matching with quick preprocessing  deep inspection was a critical strategy in many network operations  including traffic identification  intrusion detection  content based pricing  data loss prevention and so on  regular expressions were currently frequently utilized in implementing deep inspection due to their remarkable expressiveness  and almost all rules were created using regular expressions  reference  8  described how to use a pool based simulated annealing approach to learn regular expressions for explainable medical text classification  using high quality and interpretable regular expressions  a rule based engine for medical text categorization was constructed  a constructive heuristic process was used to produce the regular expressions  which were then optimized using the pool based simulated annealing  psa  methodology  although existing deep neural network  dnn  techniques perform well in the majority of natural language processing  nlp  applications  people see them as incomprehensible  black boxes   when interpretable solutions are needed  rule based techniques are often adopted  notably in the medical business  however  creating regular expressions for large datasets may be time consuming  the goal of the project was to minimize manual lab work while maintaining high quality outcomes  the pool based simulated annealing technique was suggested for automatically optimizing the performance of machine generated regular expressions without requiring human interaction     paper  9  developed learning techniques and regular expressions based pattern matching for behaviour monitoring  a unique monitoring system that combined two key anomaly detection trends  the a priori kb approach and the lb approach  was used to optimize their respective advantages  the approach was broken into two parts  classifying target behaviours into feature sequences and comparing feature sequences to reference patterns  the reference patterns were predefined based on extensive information  which may be learnt automatically using a supporting nn or both  the proposed strategy was validated by numerical simulations and tests  as well as comparisons to other well known approaches in the field  a lightweight regular expression verification system  10  was used instead of a large number of test cases  the approach employed plain language descriptions of requirements to automatically generate formal specifications  by comparing the synthesized requirements to the target regular expressions  errors were discovered and counter examples were presented  they developed a web application prototype and utilized two case studies to demonstrate its use  paper  11  used manual processing and archiving to handle and archive various unstructured court papers  the research aimed to evaluate the structure of judgments  extract judicial language entities and show cases in the form of an entity circulation map in order to make better use of them and achieve professional application  the court document  as the text carrier of unstructured public events  of higher standard format is well written and easy to analyse and so became the research focus of the work  by examining the evolution of named entity recognition technology  testing and evaluating the use of the extraction tool  gate  and assessing the cost and effectiveness in the judicial sector  the study presented a rule based regular expression approach for entity identification     in  12   a system that utilizes nlp to easily extract relevant information from a train reservation database by delivering structured natural language inquiries as input and receiving sql queries as response was proposed  tokenization  lemmatization  labelling of parts of speech  parsing and mapping are all stages in the process  the dataset used for the proposed system contained 2880 structured natural language queries on train rates and available seats  in today s fast paced technological world  individuals must interact with computers to help in a variety of fields such as medicine  education and space exploration  the process of getting relevant data from the database takes time  to extract data from a database  the user must first be acquainted with a database management system  dbms   which is software that is intended to store and administer databases     the method in  12  employed the text s language expression rules and other relevant data to generate feature word lists and a rule template that corresponds to the text  because of the rapid growth and broad use of information technology in many aspects of people s lives  massive volumes of data have become accessible  text sets  as an important means of information transport  include valuable data  information and expertise  the text set s digital data is important  but it also naturally conveys the text to the entity  dr  abul bashar proposed an in depth learning technique survey on neural networks  13   it provided a study of machine learning algorithms that goes through the many uses of new deep learning designs  such as voice recognition  picture identification  language processing and additional applications  including bot and fraud prevention and illness diagnostics  according to the assessment  even with unlabelled and incomplete information  the deep convolution neural network was an accurate technique of classifying and forecasting using grouping and ranking in feature hierarchies     dr  j  samuel manoharan proposed  14  a capsule networking algorithm towards text summarization dynamic provisioning  the proposed capsule network method successfully detected and grouped categories with comparable characteristics  the bgc dataset was built using a real world situation  in hmc tasks  capsule networks provided good qualities for increasingly integrated collections and included a large number of uncommon label combinations  algorithms are often presented with previously unknown label combinations  shakya and smys  15  suggested that in online banking  big data analytics may help with risk operation and customer segmentation  according to a recent poll  banks across the globe are not only focussed on enhancing asset quality and ensuring compliance with regulations but also looking for a responsible for developing and implementing the strategy to engage consumers in offering services and products successfully  because most data engendered in bank transfers and atm money transfers are amorphous  accounting for roughly 2 5 quintillion bits of data valid for fraudulent activities  the risk mitigation and customer experience  banks can use the latest big data analytics research methods to deal with the challenges and competitive pressure  govinda et al   16  addressed that sentiment classification is a crucial challenge in trend analysis  amazon customer expectations were chosen as the source of data for the research  a technique for categorizing sentiment scores has been developed  with thorough explanations of each stage  investigations on text summarization as well as review level categorization were conducted     3 proposed system design  the classification of regular expressions on healthcare medical dataset has been utilized  this system demonstrates the generation of regular expressions from large text and processes them using nlp and ml techniques  the modified support vector machine  msvm  algorithm has been utilized to identify regular expression text and generation on the test dataset  weka 7 3 open source java environment has been utilized to classify machine learning algorithms  the extensive healthcare review dataset has been collected from various internet sources  figure 1 demonstrates preprocessing  normalization and feature extraction techniques with nlp algorithms and classification of various machine learning algorithms     fig  1    proposed system architecture    full size image  data alignment  smith waterman  sw  method  which is extensively used in bioinformatics  has been employed  the sw algorithm finds areas of commonality between even sequences  correlation based techniques are better for equally correlated sequences  because text snippets vary in word count and duration  sw was used  red matches one snippet  main snippet  to every other string using sw  it gives good points to segments that match and unfavourable scores to portions that do not match  so  to align  he has smoked for years  with  he has been smoking for years    he  is used as a match  whereas  smoked  and  been  are incompatibilities  pairing tokens get a number equal to the lasting at least  whereas disagreement  implantation and removal tokens receive a score of 1  the total of the match  variance  insertion and deletion values are the similarity score  the score is 10 in the case below  aligning two excepts might be tricky  sw outputs the top scoring one  if a text includes numeric patterns  the digits are replaced with a  d   pattern  for example   5 10    3 10  and  7 10  have same pattern interpretation d  d      pattern builder  a data structure even without approach shots is generated for each key  the ndc version employs key phrases to build regular expressions and the  s s    pattern to allow arbitrary amount of tokens among phrases  the other  dc  variant limits the number of tokens separating sentences  token length is determined by the sequence  s s  n m  where s  is a word like grouping of non whitespace character  and n is the necessary minimum token length  red sets n and m depending on the previous alignment s token count  the dc version matches fewer unseen fragments but matches fewer false positive results  using the same example as before  the ndc variation of the phrase is  he has smoked s s   for s s   years   whereas the dc equivalent is  he has smoked s s  0 1for s s  0 1 years   he has smoked 1 pack every day for 6 or 7 years  but the dc equivalent could not be generated     the dataset contains various attributes  including the review comments of specific users  the 1155 instances have been taken for evaluating the proposed system  the 15 fold cross validation has been used for data splitting as training and testing  after feature extraction and classifier  module training generates the classification rules for specific text data  interesting remaining data has a feed to test the classifier  and it produces recommended regular expressions for actual data  finally  the similarity assessment is evaluated between actual and predicted regular expressions and the effectiveness of the proposed system has been detailed in the result section  table 1 shows the modifications done in the proposed svm over the traditional svm that does not follow this approach     table 1 svm parameter configuration  full size table  4 algorithm design  msvm    svm computes the highest margin perimeter  resulting in a homogeneous partitioning of all data attributes  on either side of the margin  sample data tagged as support vectors can be discovered  with smallest one support vector for individual class of data  these support vectors recollect the margin s peripheries and can be employed to build the hyperplane bisecting the margin  as stated in the below equation  and also to construct the hyperplane bisecting the margin in the equation               0  w  x  b 0          y mx b  the above equation represents the hyperplane and line formulas  respectively  an svm should discover weights for all selection data x such that the data points are isolated according to a determination rule  svm converts into a new space if the sample points cannot be separated linearly  the use of a kernel procedure performs this  the kernel function computes the dot product of two vectors in a new area without demanding knowledge of the transformation into that space  svms outperform other classification methods in text classification problems     nb classifier    a basic assumption of the bayes theorem is that the attributes in a given tuple are conditionally independent  as shown in equation below                1            p t ci   j 1k p tj ci   here          p tj ci  is the number of tuples of class   ci and value   tj divided by the number of tuples of class   ci  the entire function returns the values for classifier  and based on that  the final class label for each instance is decided     rf classifier    each classification tree in the random forest votes for a class  as a classification result  the class with the most votes is chosen  the randomized forest training method uses the general approach of bootstrapping aggregation or bagging  bagging periodically  b times  takes a representative selection with replenishment of the training dataset and fits branches to these measurements     step 1   assume b   1  2    b  sample n training instances from x  y with replacement     step 2   predict the future using x  y as inputs     step 3   after training  summing the forecasts from all the separate regression problems on x  may predict unknown samples x      dataset description  the drug review dataset has been used to generate the regular expression in the proposed system  the dataset contains around ten attributes  but only two characteristics in the data normalization phase  such as review comment and class type are selected  below  table 2 demonstrates a detailed description of each class with the number of instances selected for testing     table 2 number of instances taken for system testing  full size table  5 