size image  figure 2 demonstrates regular expression generation and classification using machine learning as well as proposed msvm classifier  the msvm obtains higher results than traditional naive bayes  nb   random forest  rf  and svm  several tests are conducted as a consequence of the study  each with a distinct algorithm  a single algorithm and a combination of two techniques parameter updated configuration  the integration of msvm algorithm is more efficient than a single algorithmic method  on big datasets  the prediction model has been calculated and they generated accuracy graphs that yield almost 95  accuracy     6 conclusion  due to their complexity and versatility  data structures have traditionally been utilized in text processing  the creation of fully explainable regular expressions  on the other hand  is not easy and often requires a significant investment in human by skilled employees  in order to develop regular expression based learners for medical classification tasks  a unique constructive msvm approach has been suggested  compared to traditional machine learning approaches  regular expression based classifiers increase their performance by correctly detecting many of the miscategorized examples  eliminating black boxes and producing fully interpretable answers  it is believed that employing pattern matching to tap into the chronological links between essential words is a potential strategy for improving text categorization and supporting correct decision making  by inducing generic characteristics of medical things in health care  this framework can be modified further to execute entity extraction activities  regular expressions may be used to solve information extraction problems because  in many circumstances  the essential entities follow an underlying grammatical pattern defined by regular expressions  7   an computerized method of acquaintance graph generation will be done using high quality data and medical ideas in the future as a founda