 world applications  with a realistic dataset  the model has been shown to be capable of handling medical text categorization tasks   the rest of the work is presented under the following headings  sect  2 examines the existing methods to regular expression generating techniques created by previous researchers  while sect  3 depicts the materials and techniques employed in the creation of the proposed system  and sect  4 provides the implementing algorithm explanation  in sect  5  the experimental strategy for implementing the business work and results obtained with the technology  as well as a comparison with numerous state of the art techniques  have been discussed  section 6 details the conclusion as well as its future potential   contribution of proposed work the previous work had the challenge of generating practical regular expressions on extensive data  and it regenerated dimensionality reduction issues and data leakage problems during classification  in this work  the entire work is evaluated in a systematic approach  including a new classification algorithm that improves the classification accuracy  and proposed sequence alignment and key generation approach to reduce the data leakage problem   2 literature survey natural language processing  nlp  systems designed for regular text find it challenging to interpret medical phrases spoken orally  4   to address these concerns  an automated regular expression generation approach is considered for classifying medical texts in order to deliver insightful and complete human like medical assistance   1  practical studies on diverse problems in regular expression consequence   2  test general string generation from traditional phrases   3  automatic learning or synthesis of regular expressions from illustration strings or specifications   4  statically checking the syntax or specific semantic mistakes in regular expressions or verifying regular expressions with requirements   5  the representation of visual expressions   authors of paper  1  developed regex  a regular appearance feature based approach for biomedical text categorization  regex is a standard expression based approach for identifying characteristics from text documents  using the smith waterman and compensate for the lack of sequencing matching techniques  identifiers were retrieved from the medical domain and used to indicate frequent patterns  the effectiveness of the suggested approach was evaluated using three annotations datasets  including characteristics of obesity  obesity categories and smoking behaviours  features derived from consecutive sequences of characters  n grams  were utilized as a comparative  and both kinds of features were characterized mathematically using the tf idf vector framework  the capacity of background subtraction methodologies was assessed using svm and naive bayes classifiers that were trained  according to the results  regular expression features enhanced both classifications  effectiveness in all datasets despite utilizing limited functionality than n grams  particularly in datasets with knowledge on morphological attributes  in paper  4   fault based leadership development programmes were conducted for regular expression realization using mutation  a fault based strategy for generating strings suitable for regular expression testing  they provided fault classes that characterize faults that may arise when building a regular expression  as well as the idea of a distinguishing string  which is a string that may reveal a flaw  this technique  given a regular expression  generated a test suite of distinguishing strings that detected probable regular expression defects  they demonstrated several versions of the process  each with a distinct consequence in terms of test suite size and production time   regex  a simple text categorization  was turned into an al biomedical text classifier in  5  by using a query method and stopping criteria  the query approach sampled the training dataset  balancing greedy regular expression classification precision with conservative text sequence alignment classification  a stopping benchmark is a sustained condensing in the contention of query technique scores  the al classifier was considered against support vector machine  svm   naive bayes  nb  and a classifier based on bidirectional encoder models from transformers utilizing three datasets incorporating biological knowledge in spanish on smoking demeanours  obesity and obesity varieties  as regular expressions evolve over time  the qualities of regular expression edits  syntactic and semantic distinctions and feature changes of alterations were examined  in  6   two datasets were used in the investigation  to acquire the changing history of regular expressions  they first checked through the contribution logs of github applications that incorporate one in their latest iteration  second  they compiled a list of frequent terms used by research subjects during drawback tasks  regular expression matching characteristics might be dramatically different as a consequence of a one character error  regular expressions have their own range of tools that may be used to write tests  these tools display components of the pattern matching language  but not quasi sequences  recent research has looked at a fault based technique to produce regular expression tests using mutation testing  in which flaws were injected into regular expressions and strings were produced to witness the defect  resulting in non matching instances for the original regular expression   paper  7  described a constructive heuristic approach to medical text classification using regular expressions  as text classifiers  a novel constructive heuristic technique for creating a set of regular expressions might be used  the approach s key distinguishing feature was the development of a novel  regular affirmation text classifier with adequate classification performance and good interpretability  they put the system to the test using real world medical data from one of the market s major online healthcare professionals and found that it worked effectively and consistently  computer clustering techniques were employed efficiently in combination with machine learning to conduct medical text categorization tasks  and according to findings of the experiments  in  2   a new matching engine  bfa  was introduced to provide high speed mathematical equation matching with quick preprocessing  deep inspection was a critical strategy in many network operations  including traffic identification  intrusion detection  content based pricing  data loss prevention and so on  regular expressions were currently frequently utilized in implementing deep inspection due to their remarkable expressiveness  and almost all rules were created using regular expressions  reference  8  described how to use a pool based simulated annealing approach to learn regular expressions for explainable medical text classification  using high quality and interpretable regular expressions  a rule based engine for medical text categorization was constructed  a constructive heuristic process was used to produce the regular expressions  which were then optimized using the pool based simulated annealing  psa  methodology  although existing deep neural network  dnn  techniques perform well in the majority of natural language processing  nlp  applications  people see them as incomprehensible  black boxes   when interpretable solutions are needed  rule based techniques are often adopted  notably in the medical business  however  creating regular expressions for large datasets may be time consuming  the goal of the project was to minimize manual lab work while maintaining high quality outcomes  the pool based simulated annealing technique was suggested for automatically optimizing the performance of machine generated regular expressions without requiring human interaction   paper  9  developed learning techniques and regular expressions based pattern matching for behaviour monitoring  a unique monitoring system that combined two key anomaly detection trends  the a priori kb approach and the lb approach  was used to optimize their respective advantages  the approach was broken into two parts  classifying target behaviours into feature sequences and comparing feature sequences to reference patterns  the reference patterns were predefined based on extensive information  which may be learnt automatically using a supporting nn or both  the proposed strategy was validated by numerical simulations and tests  as well as comparisons to other well known approaches in the field  a lightweight regular expression verification system  10  was used instead of a large number of test cases  the approach employed plain language descriptions of requirements to automatically generate formal specifications  by comparing the synthesized requirements to the target regular expressions  errors were discovered and counter examples were presented  they developed a web application prototype and utilized two case studies to demonstrate its use  paper  11  used manual processing and archiving to handle and archive various unstructured court papers  the research aimed to evaluate the structure of judgments  extract judicial language entities and show cases in the form of an entity circulation map in order to make better use of them and achieve professional application  the court document  as the text carrier of unstructured public events  of higher standard format is well written and easy to analyse and so became the research focus of the work  by examining the evolution of named entity recognition technology  testing and evaluating the use of the extraction tool  gate  and assessing the cost and effectiveness in the judicial sector  the study presented a rule based regular expression approach for entity identification   in  12   a system that utilizes nlp to easily extract relevant information from a train reservation database by delivering structured natural language inquiries as input and receiving sql queries as response was proposed  tokenization  lemmatization  labelling of parts of speech  parsing and mapping are all stages in the process  the dataset used for the proposed system contained 2880 structured natural language queries on train rates and available seats  in today s fast paced technological world  individuals must interact with computers to help in a variety of fields such as medicine  education and space exploration  the process of getting relevant data from the database takes time  to extract data from a database  the user must first be acquainted with a database management system  dbms   which is software that is intended to store and administer databases   the method in  12  employed the text s language expression rules and other relevant data to generate feature word lists and a rule template that corresponds to the text  because of the rapid growth and broad use of information technology in many aspects of people s lives  massive volumes of data have become accessible  text sets  as an important means of information transport  include valuable data  information and expertise  the text set s digital data is important  but it also naturally conveys the text to the entity  dr  abul bashar proposed an in depth learning technique survey on neural networks  13   it provided a study of machine learning algorithms that goes through the many uses of new deep learning designs  such as voice recognition  picture identification  language processing and additional applications  including bot and fraud prevention and illness diagnostics  according to the assessment  even with unlabelled and incomplete information  the deep convolution neural network was an accurate technique of classifying and forecasting using grouping and ranking in feature hierarchies   dr  j  samuel manoharan proposed  14  a capsule networking algorithm towards text summarization dynamic provisioning  the proposed capsule network method successfully detected and grouped categories with comparable characteristics  the bgc dataset was built using a real world situation  in hmc tasks  capsule networks provided good qualities for increasingly integrated collections and included a large number of uncommon label combinations  algorithms are often presented with previously unknown label combinations  shakya and smys  15  suggested that in online banking  big data analytics may help with risk operation and customer segmentation  according to a recent poll  banks across the globe are not only focussed on enhancing asset quality and ensuring compliance with regulations but also looking for a responsible for developing and implementing the strategy to engage consumers in offering services and products successfully  because most data engendered in bank transfers and atm money transfers are amorphous  accounting for roughly 2 5 quintillion bits of data valid for fraudulent activities  the risk mitigation and customer experience  banks can use the latest big data analytics research methods to deal with the challenges and competitive pressure  govinda et al   16  addressed that sentiment classification is a crucial challenge in trend analysis  amazon customer expectations were chosen as the source of data for the research  a technique for categorizing sentiment scores has been developed  with thorough explanations of each stage  investigations on text summarization as well as review level categorization were conducted   3 proposed system design the classification of regular expressions on healthcare medical dataset has been utilized  this system demonstrates the generation of regular expressions from large text and processes them using nlp and ml techniques  the modified support vector machine  msvm  algorithm has been utilized to identify regular expression text and generation on the test dataset  weka 7 3 open source java environment has been utilized to classify m