d as a consequence of the study  each with a distinct algorithm  a single algorithm and a combination of two techniques parameter updated configuration  the integration of msvm algorithm is more efficient than a single algorithmic method  on big datasets  the prediction model has been calculated and they generated accuracy graphs that yield almost 95  accuracy   6 conclusion due to their complexity and versatility  data structures have traditionally been utilized in text processing  the creation of fully explainable regular expressions  on the other hand  is not easy and often requires a significant investment in human by skilled employees  in order to develop regular expression based learners for medical classification tasks  a unique constructive msvm approach has been suggested  compared to traditional machine learning approaches  regular expression based classifiers increase their performance by correctly detecting many of the miscategorized examples  eliminating black boxes and producing fully interpretable answers  it is believed that employing pattern matching to tap into the chronological links between essential words is a potential strategy for improving text categorization and supporting correct decision making  by inducing generic characteristics of medical things in health care  this framework can be modified further to execute entity extraction activities  regular expressions may be used to solve information extraction problems because  in many circumstances  the essential entities follow an underlying grammatical pattern defined by regular expressions  7   an computerized method of acquaintance graph generation will be done using high quality data and medical ideas in the future as a foundation to learn high quality sources of knowledge relating to illnesses directly from computerized medical data   references flores ca  figueroa rl  pezoa je  2019  fregex  a feature extraction method for biomedical text classification using regular expressions  in  20