encoding an integer using unary coding the unary coding is a variable length in coding method  in this case  integer this 1 will be encoded as x  1  1 bit followed by 0  so for example  3 will be encoded as 2  1s followed by 0  whereas 5 will be encoded as 4  1s  followed by 0  etc 
