map s tradeoffs  the map incorporates the trade off between precision and recall and considers both false positives  fp  and false negatives  fn   this property makes map a suitable metric for most detection applications 
mean reciprocal rank the mean reciprocal rank is a statistic measure for evaluating any process that produces a list of possible responses to a sample of queries  ordered by probability of correctness  the reciprocal rank of a query response is the multiplicative inverse of the rank of the first correct answer  1 for first place  1 2 for second place  1 3 for third place and so on  the mean reciprocal rank is the average of the reciprocal ranks of results for a sample of queries q
