formula formulation of tr first  we have our vocabulary set  which is just a set of words in a language   play video starting at  7 44 and follow transcript7 44  now here  we are considering only one language  but in reality  on the web  there might be multiple natural languages  we have texts that are in all kinds of languages   play video starting at  7 57 and follow transcript7 57  but here for simplicity  we just assume that is one kind of language  as the techniques used for retrieving data from multiple languages are more or less similar to the techniques used for retrieving documents in one end  which although there is important difference  the principle methods are very similar   play video starting at  8 21 and follow transcript8 21  next  we have the query  which is a sequence of words   play video starting at  8 26 and follow transcript8 26  and so here  you can see  play video starting at  8 31 and follow transcript8 31  the query is defined as a sequence of words  each q sub i is a word in the vocabulary   play video starting at  8 42 and follow transcript8 42  a document is defined in the same way  so it s also a sequence of words  and here  d sub ij is also a word in the vocabulary   play video starting at  8 52 and follow transcript8 52  now typically  the documents are much longer than queries   play video starting at  8 57 and follow transcript8 57  but there are also cases where the documents may be very short   play video starting at  9 4 and follow transcript9 04  so you can think about what might be a example of that case   play video starting at  9 9 and follow transcript9 09  i hope you can think of twitter search  tweets are very short   play video starting at  9 16 and follow transcript9 16  but in general  documents are longer than the queries   play video starting at  9 22 and follow transcript9 22  now  then we have a collection of documents  and this collection can be very large  so think about the web  it could be very large   play video starting at  9 36 and follow transcript9 36  and then the goal of text retrieval is you ll find the set of relevant in the documents  which we denote by r  q   because it depends on the query  and this in general  a subset of all the documents in the collection   play video starting at  9 52 and follow transcript9 52  unfortunately  this set of relevant documents is generally unknown  and user dependent in the sense that  for the same query typed in by different users  they expect the relevant documents may be different   play video starting at  10 9 and follow transcript10 09  the query given to us by the user is only a hint on which document should be in this set   play video starting at  10 17 and follow transcript10 17  and indeed  the user is generally unable to specify what exactly should be in this set  especially in the case of web search  where the connection s so large  the user doesn t have complete knowledge about the whole production   play video starting at  10 34 and follow transcript10 34  so the best search system can do is to compute an approximation of this relevant document set  so we denote it by r  q   so formerly  we can see the task is to compute this r  q  approximation of the relevant documents  so how can we do that  now imagine if you are now asked to write a program to do this   play video starting at  11 8 and follow transcript11 08  what would you do  now think for a moment  right  so these are your input  the query  the documents   play video starting at  11 20 and follow transcript11 20  and then you are to compute the answers to this query  which is a set of documents that would be useful to the user   play video starting at  11 29 and follow transcript11 29  so  how would you solve the problem  now in general  there are two strategies that we can use   play video starting at  11 39 and follow transcript11 39  the first strategy is we do a document selection  and that is  we re going to have a binary classification function  or binary classifier   play video starting at  11 49 and follow transcript11 49  that s a function that would take a document and query as input  and then give a zero or one as output to indicate whether this document is relevant to the query or not   play video starting at  12 2 and follow transcript12 02  so in this case  you can see the document   play video starting at  12 8 and follow transcript12 08  the relevant document is set  is defined as follows  it basically  all the documents that have a value of 1 by this function   play video starting at  12 25 and follow transcript12 25  so in this case  you can see the system must have decide if the document is relevant or not  basically  it has to say whether it s one or zero  and this is called absolute relevance  basically  it needs to know exactly whether it s going to be useful to the user   play video starting at  12 41 and follow transcript12 41  alternatively  there s another strategy called document ranking   play video starting at  12 46 and follow transcript12 46  now in this case  the system is not going to make a call whether a document is random or not  but rather the system is going to use a real value function  f here   play video starting at  12 58 and follow transcript12 58  that would simply give us a value that would indicate which document is more likely relevant   play video starting at  13 5 and follow transcript13 05  so it s not going to make a call whether this document is relevant or not  but rather it would say which document is more likely relevant  so this function then can be used to random documents  and then we re going to let the user decide where to stop  when the user looks at the document  so we have a threshold theta here to determine what documents should be in this approximation set  and we re going to assume that all the documents that are ranked above the threshold are in this set  because in effect  these are the documents that we deliver to the user  and theta is a cutoff determined by the user   play video starting at  13 56 and follow transcript13 56  so here we ve got some collaboration from the user in some sense  because we don t really make a cutoff  and the user kind of helped the system make a cutoff   play video starting at  14 8 and follow transcript14 08  so in this case  the system only needs to decide if one document is more likely relevant than another  and that is  it only needs to determine relative relevance   play video starting at  14 19 and follow transcript14 19  as opposed to absolute relevance 
