an explanation on the applications of euclidean distance and cosine similarity cosine similarity is generally used as a metric for measuring distance when the magnitude of the vectors does not matter  this happens for example when working with text data represented by word counts  we could assume that when a word  e g  science  occurs more frequent in document 1 than it does in document 2  that document 1 is more related to the topic of science  however  it could also be the case that we are working with documents of uneven lengths  wikipedia articles for example   then  science probably occurred more in document 1 just because it was way longer than document 2  cosine similarity corrects for this 
