an explanation of bm25 ranking formula in information retrieval  bm25  bm is an abbreviation of best matching  is a ranking function used by search engines to estimate the relevance of documents to a given search query  bm25 is a bag of words retrieval function that ranks a set of documents based on the query terms appearing in each document  regardless of their proximity within the document  it is a family of scoring functions with slightly different components and parameters 
