mean reciprocal rank wiki the mean reciprocal rank is a statistic measure for evaluating any process that produces a list of possible responses to a sample of queries  ordered by probability of correctness  the reciprocal rank of a query response is the multiplicative inverse of the rank of the first correct answer  1 for first place  1 2 for second place  1 3 for third place and so on  
