explanation and code for discounted cumulative gain the discounted cumulative gain  dcg  is a relevance metric in information science and information retrieval  unlike pure classification use cases where you are right or wrong  in a ranking problem  you are more or less right or wrong  the relevance actually denotes how well the retrieved set of documents properly answers the initial query 
