an interesting article discussion weak supervision  which allows us to deal with having a large corpus of unlabeled data  shows the general approach that is helpful to take  the three steps that are important to make this approach viable with weak supervision  the user defines a set of functions and rules that assign a noisy label  that is a label that may not be correct  to unlabeled data  the labeling functions may be in the form of patterns such as regular expressions  dictionaries  ontologies  pre trained machine learning models  or crowd annotation     weak supervision pipelines have three components   1  user defined labeling functions and heuristic functions   2  a statistical model which takes as input the labels from the functions  and outputs probabilistic labels  and  3  a machine learning model that is trained on the probabilistic training labels from the statistical model     
