ndcg k   in  plain  language  the discounted cumulative gain for k shown recommendations       dcg k  sums the relevance of the shown items for the current user  cumulative   meanwhile adding a penalty for relevant items placed on later positions  discounted      the normalized cumulative gain for k shown recommendations        ndcg k  divides this score by the maximum possible value of      dcg k for the current user  i e  what the score      dcg k would be if the items in the ranking were sorted by the true  unknown for the recommender model  relevance  this is called ideal discounted cumulative gain        idcg k   so the score is normalized for different users 
