dcg assumptions discounted cumulative gain  dcg measures the usefulness  or gain  of a document based on its position in the result list  the gain is accumulated from the top of the result list to the bottom  with the gain of each result discounted at lower ranks     measure of ranking quality   used to measure effectiveness of search algorithms in information retrieval     underlying assumptions  highly relevant documents are more useful if appearing earlier in search result   highly relevant documents are more useful than marginally relevant documents which are better than non relevant documents 
