reasoning behind top k measure this is linked to theoretical and computational issues  the more classes you consider  the more you suffer from class ambiguity  classes whose members are much more similar to each other than to other classes   this is also an important issue when scaling image classification problems to a huge number of classes  and has motivated the use of loss functions that optimise the top k error instead of the zero one loss
