zip s law applications its also used often in information retrieval and nlp       zipf s law is used to compress indices for search engines based on word distribution  http   nlp stanford edu ir book html htmledition irbook html   though not always  the zipfian nature of distribution is sometimes used to normalize the importance of words in a search query  in an extension of ranking methods such as tf idf  http   en wikipedia org wiki tf idf   it is used to predict the number of times the n most popular word occurs in a corpus  or the fraction of words with frequency n   
