this page explains why pivoted normalized document length is important for normalizing document vectors in the vector space model   to this end  we introduce a form of normalizing the vector representations of documents in the collection  so that the resulting   normalized   documents are not necessarily of unit length  then  when we compute the dot product score between a  unit  query vector and such a normalized document  the score is skewed to account for the effect of document length on relevance  this form of compensation for document length is known as pivoted document length normalization      
