this page explains how to handle stop words by creating a list of the most common words and how to regard these words in document scoring   sometimes  some extremely common words which would appear to be of little value in helping select documents matching a user need are excluded from the vocabulary entirely  these words are called stop words   the general strategy for determining a stop list is to sort the terms by collection frequency  the total number of times each term appears in the document collection   and then to take the most frequent terms  often hand filtered for their semantic content relative to the domain of the documents being indexed  as a stop list
