paper about doc length normalization document length normalization adjusts the term frequency or the relevance score in order to normalize the effect of document length on the document ranking 
examples of document length normalization then  when we compute the dot product score between a  unit  query vector and such a normalized document  the score is skewed to account for the effect of document length on relevance  this form of compensation for document length is known as pivoted document length normalization  
