map vs ndcg  ndcg  normalised discounted cumulative gain  is a single number measure of effectiveness of a ranking algorithm that allows non binary relevance judgments  it has a strong relationship to the average precision  ap   but has a discounting function with a very heavy tail that must be truncated 
