pivoted length normalization formula pivoted length normalization is a formula to evaluate how relevant a query is respect to some text     if you define  d  as the document length and avdl as the average length of a document then pivoted document length normalization divides the tf idf value by     1 b b d avdl1 b b d avdl    where b is a number between 0 and 1     this penalizes longer documents  if you want to slightly reward documents for being longer then you usually add a small constant to the tf part of the calculation  this is known as bm25   lu   zhai 2011  
