the highlighted text is useful because it explains how beta impacts the tradeoff between precision and recall whenever we want to reduce the effect of false negatives  we should go for high recall and low precision  a model that produces no false negatives will have a recall of 100    whenever we want to reduce the effect of false positives  we should go for low recall and high precision  a model that produces no false positives will have precision of 100  
