stages of vector space model the vector space model procedure can be divided in to three stages  the first stage is the document indexing where content bearing terms are extracted from the document text  the second stage is the weighting of the indexed terms to enhance retrieval of document relevant to the user  the last stage ranks the document with respect to the query according to a similarity measure  a common similarity measure known as cosine measure determines angle between the document vector and the query vector  
