what is f score in statistical analysis of binary classification  the f score or f measure is a measure of a test s accuracy  it is calculated from the precision and recall of the test  where the precision is the number of true positive results divided by the number of all positive results  including those not identified correctly  and the recall is the number of true positive results divided by the number of all samples that should have been identified as positive  precision is also known as positive predictive value  and recall is also known as sensitivity in diagnostic binary classification 
