explanation of the cranfield paradigm and test collections for ir model a real user application  with realistic information needs collect enough documents and create enough topics to allow significant testing on results make relevance judgments before the experiments  this prevents human bias and enables re usability define metrics that reflect real user situations run strategy a and b evaluate a and b using appropriate metrics compare a with b statistically state whether a works better than b  a and b are equivalent  or b works better than a the cranfield paradigm today
