zipf s law definition zipf s law   z f   german   ts  pf   is an empirical law formulated using mathematical statistics that refers to the fact that for many types of data studied in the physical and social sciences  the rank frequency distribution is an inverse relation  the zipfian distribution is one of a family of related discrete power law probability distributions  it is related to the zeta distribution  but is not identical 
