performance of inverted indices in information retrieval systems the performance of distributed text document retrieval systems is strongly influenced by the organization of the inverted index  this paper compares the performance impact on query processing of various physical organizations for inverted lists  we present a new probabilistic model of the database and queries  simulation experiments determine which variables most strongly injluence response time and throughput  this leads to a set of design trade offs over a range of hardware configurations and new parallel query processing strategies
