this article breaks down the computation need of vector space model outlining the approach and considers efficiency and security of big data search engines  computational analysis and understanding of natural languages  principles  methods and applications  venkat n  gudivada      amogh r  gudivada  in handbook of statistics  2018    9 vector space ir model  the vector space model  vsm  is based on the notion of similarity  the model assumes that the relevance of a document to query is roughly equal to the document query similarity  both the documents and queries are represented using the bag of words model  for a document collection  we first determine a set of terms  i e   vocabulary  and order the terms  next  documents are represented as n dimensional vectors  where each dimension corresponds to a term  terms are weighted using tf idf or bm25 methods  queries are also represented as n dimensional vectors     fig  8 shows a three dimensional vector space spanned by three terms data  analytics  and learning  there are three documents d1  d2  and d3 and corresponding to each document is a three dimensional vector  denoted d1  d2   and d3   the term weights of d1  are  w11  w12  w13   the term weights determine the document s orientation placement in the vector space  like documents  queries are also represented as three dimensional vectors  query q  w1 w2 w3  in fig  8   and the query terms can also be weighted 
