full text search is antoher approach where look for specific features in given text and draws into the text mining strategies utilized to build large search systems for users to obtain relevant data for their needs  full text search refers to searching some text inside extensive text data stored electronically and returning results that contain some or all of the words from the query  in contrast  traditional search would return exact matches     while traditional databases are great for storing and retrieving general data  performing full text searches has been challenging  frequently  additional tooling is required to achieve this     in this article  you will learn what a full text search is  how it works  and how to implement it in mongodb 
