why stop words are critical to many applications the reason why stop words are critical to many applications is that  if we remove the words that are very commonly used in a given language  we can focus on the important words instead  for example  in the context of a search engine  if your search query is  how to develop information retrieval applications   if the search engine tries to find web pages that contained the terms  how    to   develop    information    retrieval    applications  the search engine is going to find a lot more pages that contain the terms  how    to  than pages that contain information about developing information retrieval applications because the terms  how  and  to  are so commonly used in the english language  if we disregard these two terms  the search engine can actually focus on retrieving pages that contain the keywords   develop   information   retrieval   applications    which would bring up pages that are actually of interest  this is just the basic intuition for using stop words 
