what are the two assumptions made by the probability ranking principle  a second kind of models are called probabilistic models  in this family of models  we follow a very different strategy  where we assume that queries and documents are all observations from random variables   play video starting at  2 36 and follow transcript2 36  and we assume there is a binary random variable called r here  play video starting at  2 42 and follow transcript2 42  to indicate whether a document is relevant to a query   play video starting at  2 46 and follow transcript2 46  we then define the score of document with respect to a query as a probability that this random variable r is equal to 1  given a particular document query  there are different cases of such a general idea  one is classic probabilistic model  another is language model  yet another is divergence from randomness model 
