understanding document frequency document frequency  this measures the importance of documents in a whole set of the corpus  this is very similar to tf but the only difference is that tf is the frequency counter for a term t in document d  whereas df is the count of occurrences of term t in the document set n  in other words  df is the number of documents in which the word is present  we consider one occurrence if the term is present in the document at least once  we do not need to know the number of times the term is present 
