explained  bag of words  a bag of words model  or bow for short  is a way of extracting features from text for use in modeling  such as with machine learning algorithms     the approach is very simple and flexible  and can be used in a myriad of ways for extracting features from documents     a bag of words is a representation of text that describes the occurrence of words within a document  it involves two things     a vocabulary of known words   a measure of the presence of known words   it is called a  bag  of words  because any information about the order or structure of words in the document is discarded  the model is only concerned with whether known words occur in the document  not where in the document 
