important element of average precision is that it is based on the total number of relevant documents not the total number of documents  and then  finally  we take the average  so  we divide it by ten  and which is the total number of relevant documents in the collection   play video starting at  12 41 and follow transcript12 41  note that here  we re not dividing this sum by four  which is a number retrieved relevant documents  now  imagine  if i divide by four  what would happen   play video starting at  12 54 and follow transcript12 54  now  think about this  for a moment   play video starting at  12 57 and follow transcript12 57  it s a common mistake that people  sometimes  overlook   play video starting at  13 2 and follow transcript13 02  right  so  if we  we divide this by four  it s actually not very good  in fact  that you are favoring a system  that would retrieve very few random documents  as in that case  the denominator would be very small  so  this would be  not a good matching  so  note that this denomina  denominator is ten  the total number of relevant documents  and  this will basically  compute the area  and the needs occur  and  this is the standard method  used for evaluating a ranked list 
