a great example to demonstrate how to calculate normalized dcg given a set of documents example edit   presented with a list of documents in response to a search query  an experiment participant is asked to judge the relevance of each document to the query  each document is to be judged on a scale of 0 3 with 0 meaning not relevant  3 meaning highly relevant  and 1 and 2 meaning  somewhere in between   for the documents ordered by the ranking algorithm as      displaystyle d_ 1  d_ 2  d_ 3  d_ 4  d_ 5  d_ 6    the user provides the following relevance scores       displaystyle 3 2 3 0 1 2   that is  document 1 has a relevance of 3  document 2 has a relevance of 2  etc  the cumulative gain of this search result listing is       displaystyle  mathrm  cg_ 6     sum _ i 1   6 rel_ i  3 2 3 0 1 2 11   changing the order of any two documents does not affect the cg measure  if   displaystyle d_ 3   and   displaystyle d_ 4   are switched  the cg remains the same  11  dcg is used to emphasize highly relevant documents appearing early in the result list  using the logarithmic scale for reduction  the dcg for each result in order is         displaystyle i    displaystyle rel_ i     displaystyle  log _ 2  i 1     displaystyle   frac  rel_ i    log _ 2  i 1      1 3 1 3  2 2 1 585 1 262  3 3 2 1 5  4 0 2 322 0  5 1 2 585 0 387  6 2 2 807 0 712  so the   displaystyle dcg_ 6   of this ranking is       displaystyle  mathrm  dcg_ 6     sum _ i 1   6   frac  rel_ i    log _ 2  i 1    3 1 262 1 5 0 0 387 0 712 6 861   now a switch of   displaystyle d_ 3   and   displaystyle d_ 4   results in a reduced dcg because a less relevant document is placed higher in the ranking  that is  a more relevant document is discounted more by being placed in a lower rank     the performance of this query to another is incomparable in this form since the other query may have more results  resulting in a larger overall dcg which may not necessarily be better  in order to compare  the dcg values must be normalized     to normalize dcg values  an ideal ordering for the given query is needed  for this example  that ordering would be the monotonically decreasing sort of all known relevance judgments  in addition to the six from this experiment  suppose we also know there is a document   displaystyle d_ 7   with relevance grade 3 to the same query and a document   displaystyle d_ 8   with relevance grade 2 to that query  then the ideal ordering is       displaystyle 3 3 3 2 2 2 1 0   the ideal ranking is cut again to length 6 to match the depth of analysis of the ranking       displaystyle 3 3 3 2 2 2   the dcg of this ideal ordering  or idcg  ideal dcg    is computed to rank 6       displaystyle  mathrm  idcg_ 6    8 740   and so the ndcg for this query is given as       displaystyle  mathrm  ndcg_ 6      frac  dcg_ 6   idcg_ 6      frac  6 861  8 740   0 785 
