reddit cs410 press j to jump to the feed  press question mark to learn the rest of the keyboard shortcuts  jump to content  search within r uiuc_mcs  r uiuc_mcs    log in  sign up    user account menu  r uiuc_mcs  posts    12    posted by  u 491450451  2 years ago    review of cs 410 text information systems fall 2020  lecture video quality  8 10    assignment quality  6 10    overall difficulty  5 10    workload   5 to 8 hours    language used  python for assignments  no language restriction on project     grading  generous    exam  1 midterm and 1 final    comment  highly suggest you take the course if you are interested in statistical nlp     among 6 courses i ve taken  cs 410 text information systems is right in the middle in terms of quality and overall difficulty  the major topics 410 covers is only about statistical nlp and text retrieval  two of which are closely related  so let s say it s just about nlp  if you are looking for deep nlp e g  bert  lstm  etc  avoid this course  you won t get what you want  i was quite disappointed there is no deep nlp covered in the course at first  but after finishing it  i found statistical nlp is more general and almost universal to solve some high level problems  topics mining  sentimental analysis   though statistical nlp has been outdated     lecture videos are great in terms of how professor zhai put videos together  there is a crystal clear structure going from the start till the end  so you won t get lost in the middle and baffled by what i am learning and where i am  sometimes i had some hard time to fathom what prof  zhai refers to in the video  but the video subtitle is quite refined by students as an extra credit activity  overall  prof  zhai did a great job on the video  a minor complaint is that the video seems to be outdated  hope prof  zhai can spend last few weeks dedicating to deep nlp in the future     assignment is light and mostly autograded  most of them are based on an outdated package called metapy developed by uiuc students  this is the only major complaint i have about the course  it s obvious nltk is more popular    why not just use nltk as the default library so we don t have to re learn out of the program  it s not a big deal at all  but definitely something the instructor and tas can improve if not compromising the quality of instruction  quizzes and exams are quite tricky sometimes  since you got 3 2 tries for quizzes  so it s really not that hard to get 100   the biggest hinderance is probably exam  some simple calculation   tricky concept question  and final project  which can include implementing an algorithm from papers  competition and educationalweb  etc  overall  learnt a lot in the final project     difficulty is moderate  you got 3 2 tries for quizzes  so it s really not that hard to get 100   final project depends on how much you want to get out of it  otherwise it should be very approachable  exams have some simple calculation   tricky concept question  overall concepts are largely based on statistics  if you have strong stats  you should be totally fine     workload is light  you probably need 2 hours on video  3 hours on each coding assignment   quizzes  big project at the second part of course may take more time  otherwise  it s pretty light     recommendation  i am pretty positive the program will have deep nlp course in the future  it might benefit all students as well as catch up the trend to introduce deep nlp at the end of the course to create smooth transition  otherwise students will really feel like they are learning something from their great grandfather s generation  i also recommend add one more project in the first half of the course to further enhance the application of the course  mps are quite straightforward without any steep learning curve     8 comments    share    save    hide    report  88  upvoted  u adobe     promoted  make animated banners fast  introducing adobe express   adobe com express  learn more    comment      