formal definition of relevance feedback relevance feedback is the name given to a process where  based on user feedback about documents retrieved in an initial ranking  the system automatically modifies the description of the information need  i e  the query  and produces a new document ranking  user feedback usually takes the form of simple yes no judgements on the relevance of documents  although more detailed feedback about concepts in those documents is also possible 612 relevance feedback is a well established and effective technique in ir  and any discussion of retrieval models would be incomplete without it 
