how to build a inverted index to gain the speed benefits of indexing at retrieval time  we have to build the index in advance  the major steps in this are     collect the documents to be indexed          tokenize the text  turning each document into a list of tokens            do linguistic preprocessing  producing a list of normalized tokens  which are the indexing terms           index the documents that each term occurs in by creating an inverted index  consisting of a dictionary and postings   we will define and discuss the earlier stages of processing  that is  steps 1 3  in section 2 2  page    until then you can think of tokens and normalized tokens as also loosely equivalent to words  here  we assume that the first 3 steps have already been done  and we examine building a basic inverted index by sort based indexing      
