why testing for statistical significance is important statistical significance helps you determine the level of risk you re willing to accept  and you can balance the desire for accuracy with the resources you have available      for instance  higher statistical significance requires a larger sample size  all things being equal   so if you re willing to accept a greater risk that your results were caused by random chance  you can get away with running tests with a smaller sample size  this is often necessary when website traffic is low and it takes longer to build up a large sample size 
